Package: kilobyte-transition
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Kilobyte contributors <kilobyte@users.noreply.github.com>
Section: x11
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/jgm240/kilobyte
Depends: bash, dialog, mc, python3, python3-pyte, sudo, kbd, procps, curl, file, systemd
Recommends: elinks, sc-im, calcurse, htop, bc, bsdgames, moon-buggy, alpine, weechat, luit, telnet,
 openssh-client, newsboat, unison, gnuchess, nudoku, frotz, dict-wn, kiwix-tools, mpv, ffmpeg,
 quickjs, yt-dlp, poppler-utils, gpm, alsa-utils, unzip, zip, restic, gtypist, lrzsz
Description: Kilobyte, the text-mode desktop, next to your normal desktop
 Kilobyte is a desktop made of text: a Program Manager with an editor,
 spreadsheet, web browser, email, file manager, news feeds, games and more,
 all in the terminal. This package adds it to a normal Debian, Ubuntu or
 Raspberry Pi OS, on a text console of its own, and the command kb to move
 between the two:
 .
   kb open             go to Kilobyte
   kb close            go back to the desktop
   kb autolaunch on    start the computer into Kilobyte
   kb autolaunch off   start the computer into the desktop again
